REACHABILITY (all verified, not assumed):
- Entry point is anonymous. src/proxy.ts:99-112 rewrites any non-reserved subdomain to this route: `url.pathname = "/api/v1/proxy/" + subdomain + pathname; return NextResponse.rewrite(url, ...)`. The auth block at src/proxy.ts:155 only covers `/dashboard` and `/new`; the route handler itself calls no getSession()/checkProjectAccess(). Only control is 100 req/min/IP/path rate limiting (src/proxy.ts:122-124). The path is also directly hittable as /api/v1/proxy/<slug>/<path>.
- `targetUrl` is not user-settable — src/lib/db.ts:991 creates `productionUrl: null` and the only writer is src/lib/deployment.ts:136-138 `await updateProject(projectId, { productionUrl: effectiveUrl })` with `effectiveUrl` = the Cloud Run service URL. So the *initial* URL is safe; the redirect is what supplies the attacker-controlled URL.
- The redirect body is attacker-controlled by construction: the target is the tenant's own container running tenant-pushed code, deployed public — src/lib/gcp/cloudbuild.ts:377 `'--allow-unauthenticated'` and :420 `add-iam-policy-binding ... --member="allUsers" --role="roles/run.invoker"`. Any GitHub OAuth signup (src/app/api/auth/github) can deploy an app that answers `302 Location: <anything>`. No admin, no dev env var, no MOCK_DB (the MOCK_DB branch at line 146 is skipped in prod).
- Platform runs on Cloud Run with an ambient SA (Dockerfile `ENV NODE_ENV=production`, `EXPOSE 8080`, node server.js; src/lib/gcp/auth.ts:22-27 fetches `http://metadata.google.internal/computeMetadata/v1/instance/service-accounts/default/token` with `{'Metadata-Flavor':'Google'}`).

